{"seq":19,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T07:14:47.489Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"3a9e20000f9e0a8fa28f4a7c45d1c3bdd9ed52c7cc2659dd7c1b23489ae600ce","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Tobias, I found three ticket numbers that look like Marrow Fieldworks. None of them is labelled with the account name, though, so check the links before the call.\n\n**From Moss's notes**\n- **#4409**: in Moss's Central handoffs digest dated 2 Jan 2026. It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard. It hits Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake.\n- **#4412**: same digest. It's a small glitch with the driver SMS prompt when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots.\n\nThat digest says Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Mon 5 Jan. Hollis flagged both tickets as still open on \"Pree's dealer account\" before the handoff. I'm assuming that's Fieldworks because of where they sit, but the note never names the account next to the tickets. It also doesn't say who took the account over. Both tickets were open as of 2 Jan, and I don't know their status now.\n\n**From #central-random**\n- **#8841**: your own message on 13 Oct. You flagged that the West yard Door 2 double-books when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk at the Plains depots. Hollis had asked about the tractor-bay alerts on \"Tobias's dealer account.\" That fits Fieldworks if you took it over in January, but the channel doesn't name it.\n\n**Not Fieldworks, so I left them out**\n- FR-882 (Moss's digest) and PD-4821 (#central-team) are both Marrow Agrisupply, which is a separate account.\n\nThere are no account files for Marrow Fieldworks that I can see, so I couldn't check any of this against a CRM or ticket record."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
